{
  "name": "bb_boat_shed",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "bonebight",
  "notes": "A boat shed, 15 m by 8 m under a 45 degree silver shingle roof 8.5 m to the ridge, on a bone-block sill. Faces local -Z with a 4.5 m by 3.75 m double door standing open, its leaves swung back against the front wall. Inside, a 10 m boat is half built on stocks along the long axis: a driftwood keel and curved frames with planking on the lower half, beside a workbench, a steam box and a plank stack. Carves its interior.",
